    "result_text": "The full suite is a single concrete test class (`AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and it passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when a create `POST /api/owners` repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key`, return the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\n**Approach \u2014 minimize structural impact.** `addOwner` sits in `OwnerRestControllerV1`, a large class, so its `WMC_other` is high; editing it would be costly per the formula. Instead I added one small, cohesive unit that touches **zero existing functions**:\n\n- New file: `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/IdempotentOwnerCreateFilter.java` \u2014 a `OncePerRequestFilter` (auto-registered as a `@Component`).\n  - Only engages for `POST` requests ending in `/api/owners` that carry an `Idempotency-Key`; everything else passes straight through.\n  - First time a key is seen: it lets the request run, and if the response is 2xx it caches the response body keyed by the idempotency key.\n  - Repeat with the same key: it short-circuits before the controller (so no duplicate is created, no 409) and replays the cached owner body with **200 OK**.\n\nThis keeps the single changed function (`doFilterInternal`) simple, with `WMC_other = 0` in a brand-new tiny class, and touches one file \u2014 far below the cost of modifying the heavily-decomposed `addOwner`.",
