    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. Note that this flow is far more involved than a conventional Spring create endpoint \u2014 validation and mutation happen across a filter, two validation layers, the controller, and JPA lifecycle callbacks.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Servlet filter (before the controller)\n\n**`IdempotentOwnerCreateFilter`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/IdempotentOwnerCreateFilter.java`)\n1. If the request has an `Idempotency-Key` header **and** the key was seen before \u2192 replays the cached body with `200 OK` and short-circuits (controller never runs).\n2. Otherwise proceeds, then caches the response body for 2xx responses under that key.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Security (only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; default is `false`)\n3. `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the method requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (Because `@Valid` binding runs *before* method invocation, a 400 validation error is raised before this 403 check.)\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Request-body validation (two layers, both accumulate into one 400)\n\n**3a. Bean Validation (JSR-380) on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (generated DTO):\n4. `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n5. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(letters + up to 2 space/'/- separated parts)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n6. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(similar, optional trailing '.')`, `@Size(1..30)`\n7. `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n8. `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n9. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n10. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n11. `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n12. `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n\n**3b. Custom `OwnerFieldsValidator`** (registered via `@InitBinder` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`) \u2014 this both **mutates and validates**, in this order:\n13. **[side-effect]** Composes `address` from `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`) or falls back to `address`, run through `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, UPPERCASE, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n14. Rejects blank/whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` (\"must not be blank\").\n15. **[side-effect]** Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (strips separators, prepends `+61` dropping a leading `0`); validates 8\u201315 digits (exactly 11 for `+61`/`+1`) \u2192 sets normalized value or rejects.\n16. **[side-effect]** Lower-cases `email`.\n17. Rejects disposable-email domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n18. Postcode-vs-city region check (Sydney 2000\u20132099 / Melbourne 3000\u20133099 / Brisbane 4000\u20134099).\n19. `registrationDate` must not be in the future.\n\nAny failure here \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 `400` ProblemDetail.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Controller body (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`)\n20. MapStruct maps the (now-mutated) DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity.\n21. Loads all existing non-deleted owners.\n22. **Daily-limit gate** \u2192 `429` if \u2265100 owners already registered today (business-day-adjusted).\n23. **[side-effect]** Assigns `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n24. **Conflict gates \u2192 `409`** if any of: exact identity duplicate (`telephone|email|householdId`); same household without `sharesHousehold=true`; city already at \u226550 owners.\n25. **[side-effect]** Sets `possibleDuplicateOf` (earliest owner in same household with a different phone, unless `sharesHousehold`).\n26. **[side-effect]** Sets `namesakeCount` (existing owners with same first+last name).\n27. **[side-effect]** Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, de-duplicated with `-2`, `-3`\u2026 suffixes.\n28. Calls `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Service + JPA persistence\n29. `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` \u2014 `@Transactional`, delegates to `ownerRepository.save`.\n30. **[side-effect] `@PrePersist`**: if `registrationDate` is null, defaults to today, then rolls forward past weekends/2026 holidays (`BusinessDays.roll`).\n31. **Entity-level Bean Validation at flush**: `address`, `city`, `firstName`, `lastName` `@NotEmpty`; `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` (a second validation layer).\n32. DB insert with generated `id`.\n33. **[side-effect] `@PostPersist`** (`OwnerAuditListener`): emits an audit-log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membership level/number).\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 Response\n34. Maps entity \u2192 `OwnerDto` with many **output-only** derived fields (displayName, initials, membership fields, contactPreference, selfLink, etc.).\n35. Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if >80 owners already registered today.\n36. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns `201 CREATED`.\n37. (On the way out, the filter from step 1 caches this 2xx body if an idempotency key was supplied.)\n\n---\n\n**Not present / not applicable:** no password encoding (owners carry no credentials), no application events published, no MVC `HandlerInterceptor`, and the `CallMonitoringAspect` is never registered as a bean (and targets `@Repository` classes anyway), so no aspect runs on this path."
